  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIHR RIGHT1: Transforming the Treatment and Prevention of Leprosy and Buruli ulcers in Low and Middle-Income Countries (LMICs)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. To improve self-care in the community for patients who are at risk of recurring leprosy ulcers. 
2. To better understand the needs of patients with Buruli ulcer and the barriers to meeting those needs. 
3. To develop new and improved methods of clinical care for both leprosy and Buruli ulcer patients.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A UK and low- and middle-income country (LMIC) research partnership that aims to improve care and reduce stigma and social isolation for leprosy and Buruli ulcer in Nepal, India and Nigeria.</narrative>
  </description>
